<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-adoption-readiness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Table-driven valid and planted-defect cases prove that re-express-ready requires complete digest-bound V3 relevance, typed connectivity, nonduplication, licence and layer decisions, applicable adverse-lesson mitigation, test and currentness bindings, steady-state burden ceilings and unattended lifecycle applicability; missing, disconnected, duplicate, stale, unmitigated and over-ceiling candidates fail closed to defer or unresolved, exhaustive discovery alone never satisfies the gate, and no inventory disposition mutates V3 graph authority." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-adoption-readiness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-command-refusals> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Table-driven valid and planted-defect cases prove graph inspect, inventory, coverage, export and import bounds, explicit layer and profile selection, containment, deterministic receipts, candidate nonauthority, complete candidate diffs against an explicit accepted baseline, exhaustive exact-byte metadata-only extraction of tracked artifacts, all closed manifest selections, structured semantic documents, named resources, type and predicate vocabulary, rules and Factory records, indexed compact disposition resolution, tracked three-artifact coverage without historical roots, and zero remote contact." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-command-refusals> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-graph-structural-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "One table-driven invariant family proves stable summary and full graph inspection, explicit manifest, profile and layer closure, relation direction, denominator and nearest-rank statistic definitions, duplicate and cardinality detection, typed orphan classification, work and semantic-stage cycle refusal, predecessor-first ordering, reachability, contract-to-work, requirement, acceptance, evidence, proof, permission and validation coverage, declared layer isolation, sound parallelism bounds, write-conflict serialization and bounded execution. Planted missing, self, cyclic, disconnected, duplicate, stale, direction-reversed, closure-leaking and undeclared-crossing cases fail for exact reason codes; intentional roots, descriptive outliers and declared unknown or not-applicable dimensions warn without authorizing work. Core and product results preserve directional isolation, and unrelated graph movement leaves unaffected scoped results unchanged." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-graph-structural-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-hermetic-reproducibility> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A clean-clone test begins with empty ignored state, acquires the exact integrity-pinned lockfile artefact closure once from the allowed package registry with install scripts disabled, and then reproduces the accepted semantic digest and all required checks offline with no historical checkout, sibling repository, semantic server, pre-warmed remote cache, GitHub, provider or network-service access; a separately supplied historical-source rescan remains bounded, read-only and candidate-only, and unavailable historical bytes are reported as not independently re-extracted rather than inferred as current or complete." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-hermetic-reproducibility> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-isolation-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Core and product exports are disjoint by declared layer and versioned profile, directional scoped digests change only for relevant semantic resources, and unrelated Git or graph movement preserves current work and proof." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-isolation-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-performance-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Ten-run clean-host measurements satisfy the declared ceilings with bounded deterministic fixtures, and each retained test owns a distinct semantic rule or process boundary with subsumed assertions removed." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-performance-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-qualification-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Planted Factory behaviour defects fail for stable semantic reasons while the implementation remains independent of historical paths, Factory source, external Stardog, GitHub availability, signatures and V2 handover machinery." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-qualification-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-recovery-coverage> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The exact tracked source-set, accepted metadata inventory and reviewed recovery-decision schemas, versions and digests bind complete tracked-tree and closed manifest-union coverage for V1, V2 and every readable Factory release separately from named-resource, blank-node-component, type-vocabulary, predicate-vocabulary, referenced-IRI, rule, structured-document, test-obligation and Factory-record coverage. Verification rebinds immutable revision, tree, file and byte counts, licence boundaries, extractor profile and candidate-kind totals and rederives the complete canonical candidate family from retained tracked, manifest, RDF and structured-record metadata so a shortened inventory with recomputed summaries and digest fails. Every canonical candidate identity resolves through an exact row or deterministic indexed compact rule to exactly one disposition and provenance outcome; the V1-only report is explicitly raw source-identity delta, semantic splits and merges are reviewed mappings, and omitted, ambiguous, conflicting, duplicate, stale, unlicensed or unresolved coverage fails closed." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-recovery-coverage> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-single-path> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "All graph commands and semantic-store callers consume the same graph-manifest version 2 expansion and produce identical canonical dataset and source digests for the same tracked input." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-single-path> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-source-profile> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Table-driven equivalent literal escape, Unicode escape, line-ending, source-order and import-order forms produce identical semantic and graph digests but retain different exact source digests; an empty dataset has empty canonical bytes; semantic duplicates and every unsupported Turtle, blank-node, datatype, language-tag, RDF-star, graph-mismatch and invalid-UTF-8 form fail closed through the single loader." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-source-profile> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-tooling-fixtures> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Exact-byte synthetic V1 and V2 YAML manifests, Turtle and TriG graphs, SPARQL rules and Factory YAML and JSON records prove exhaustive tracked-artifact, commit/tree/mode/blob binding, closed manifest-union, named-resource, blank-node-component-digest, type, predicate, reference, rule and structured-record extraction plus independently contextualized exact and indexed compact-rule disposition resolution. Planted omitted or substituted blobs, forged copied runtime provenance, omitted RDF statements, structured records, documents, tests and manifest entries; repeated graph and order values; retired no-file, inactive, fixture and rule-without-output entries; parser ambiguity, aliases, duplicate keys, unsupported syntax, digest, revision, tree, count and filter drift; recomputed shortened inventories; candidate-family reverse-parity loss; forged or serialized authority context; restricted licence, empty lessons, target mismatch, stale currentness, unknown or over-ceiling burden; unsafe lifecycle; multi-discriminator compact rules, incomparable rules and every item, byte, depth and deadline ceiling fail closed without reading the historical repositories." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
