<urn:usf:policy:historical-source-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "historical-source-dependency" <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:policy:historical-source-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:enforcement> "Enforced rather than asserted. The containment check runs as a graph-declared validation and refuses any tracked runtime-bearing content that names a historical repository, worktree, recovery directory or removed system installation; a V1/V2 executable; a V1/V2 package or module import; historical runtime state; or any absolute development-machine path. It exempts five provenance documents, each of which must exist and, unless it is the programme document or the verifier itself, must carry the provenance classification marker, so an exemption cannot outlive its file or quietly become something other than a provenance document. Every rule and both exemption guards are planted-defect proven. A fresh clone with no historical source present reproduces the full test suite and all three facet verdict digests byte-identically." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:policy:historical-source-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "no-historical-source-is-required-for-any-declared-v3-path" <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:policy:historical-source-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "retaining-the-extraction-tooling-is-not-a-dependency-on-the-historical-sources" <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:policy:historical-source-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:retainedCapability> "The semantic manifest store and the recovery tooling are retained complete, sixteen and seven declared outputs all landed. They are what would reproduce the V1 and V2 accounting from the pinned sources, so the accounting's counts remain checkable rather than merely asserted. Removing them would make the corpus tidier and its historical claims weaker." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:policy:historical-source-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:retainedProvenance> "The pinned source set, with its revisions, tree digests, selection modes and licence boundaries, is retained and is read by no source file. It is the audit trail that makes an independent re-extraction possible and bounded." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:policy:historical-source-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:retainsWork> <urn:usf:work:semantic-manifest-store> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:policy:historical-source-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:retainsWork> <urn:usf:work:semantic-recovery-tooling> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:policy:historical-source-dependency:1> <urn:usf:predicate:rule> "The V1, V2 and Factory sources are optional re-verification inputs and are never required. No build, test, graph inspection, runtime, business-as-usual operation, currentness derivation or acceptance may depend on their presence." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
