<urn:usf:proof:semantic-recovery-exchange> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Exact candidate bytes pass the single manifest path, bounded exact-byte recovery extractor, tracked source-boundary plus accepted-inventory plus reviewed-decision coverage, independently contextualized adoption gate, layer isolation, directional currentness, performance and Factory behaviour fixtures under an empty ignored state without any historical checkout, sibling repository, semantic server, cache, runner, provider or network contact." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:proof:semantic-recovery-exchange> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CompletionProofObligation> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:proof:semantic-recovery-exchange> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:ProofObligation> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-adoption-readiness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Treat exhaustive historical coverage as discovery only. Compile readiness against one independent authority context derived by the recovery library from an explicitly loaded unified V3 manifest, exact versioned profile and machine-readable typed graph resources plus the exact validated source-set contract; a serialized, cloned or caller-constructed context is not compiler ingress. Never accept V3 selection, adverse-lesson denominator, licence clearance, typed connectivity, review allowlists, new-root exceptions or burden ceilings authored by the recovery decisions file itself. A re-express-ready exact disposition requires one reviewed source-digest-bound readiness record that identifies an unsatisfied exact V3 contract, requirement or consumer and rejects duplication; binds its target to a graph-derived typed connectivity receipt in the exact selected versioned V3 closure or an explicitly accepted new-root receipt with intended consumers; covers the fixed applicable adverse-lesson, retirement, supersession, defect and operational-failure denominator with explicit mitigations; obeys the pinned source licence and core-product isolation policy; and compares observations against graph-defined steady-state ceilings for authority and storage dependencies, network and provider use, update triggers, scan bytes and runtime, memory, test and maintenance cost, failure, rollback and retirement. It also records whether registered unattended usf start, status and stop lifecycle behavior is applicable and, when applicable, requires bounded retry, drain and restart with no partial authority mutation. Missing, vacuous, unknown, stale, disconnected, target-mismatched, duplicate, unmitigated or over-ceiling dimensions force defer or unresolved. A later selective V3-authored graph slice must bind the readiness-record digest and cannot infer readiness from exhaustive coverage, historical existence or current implementation." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-adoption-readiness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-candidate-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Define canonical candidate identity as the exact tuple source-set-digest, logical-source-id, pinned-source-revision, selected-file-graph-or-registry-id, candidate-kind, candidate-IRI-path-or-registry-key and discriminator, where kind covers tracked source artifact, graph or rule selection, named semantic resource, RDF type assertion, predicate vocabulary, referenced IRI, structured schema or registry record, test obligation and semantic document. Report tracked-source and manifest-selection coverage separately from candidate dispositions; each tracked file and manifest entry is covered once and every canonical candidate resolves to exactly one disposition. A compact rule must specify exact source selection and candidate kind plus at most one exact type, predicate or path class; pre-index those closed keys so resolution is linear in candidates plus rules rather than their product. Exact rows override rules, re-express-ready is forbidden from rules, stale zero-match rules fail, and ambiguous overlap or unmatched candidates fail closed." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-candidate-identity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-coverage-command> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Register read-only usf graph coverage --sources config/semantic-recovery-sources.json --inventory config/semantic-recovery-inventory.json --recovery config/semantic-recovery.json with optional --domain ID and bounded --max-items N. Rebind all three tracked artifacts to the exact current unified V3 graph authority context and report total source, semantic-resource, type-vocabulary, predicate-vocabulary, rule and Factory-record disposition coverage; distinguish durable Foundation definition coverage from current operational implementation, preserve unknown distinct from zero, never load historical source bytes, and refuse coordinated omission, stale digest, self-authored authority context, incomplete, ambiguous or duplicate resolved coverage." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-coverage-command> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-directional-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Compute separate content-only scoped dependency digests for core-to-product and product-to-core influence, bind each digest to exact selected resources and profile version, and invalidate only the affected direction so Git carrier movement and unrelated semantic change do not require reproof." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-directional-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-exchange-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Export canonical N-Quads only and place import candidates and exports beneath ignored private .usf paths using contained atomic owner-only writes; emit bounded receipts rather than bulk graph bytes on standard output. Ordinary inspect, coverage, export and import use no network, GitHub, provider, Stardog or historical path; only explicit graph inventory may read its bounded selected local legacy inputs and it persists metadata rather than RDF payloads." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-exchange-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-external-systems-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use contained local .usf candidates for copy-on-write semantic change. Treat Stardog as an optional disposable projection and GitHub only as a carrier and history service; neither availability, server statistics, workflow status nor commit identity may define semantic authority, currentness or ordinary work readiness." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-external-systems-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-factory-qualification-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Recreate only behaviour-level V2 Factory qualification in original TypeScript tests: absence never authorizes, canonical inventory fixes the denominator, exact digests and counts fail closed, closed action states cannot infer PROCEED, currentness is exact, and registry, plan, output and receipt parity are deterministic; do not copy Factory source, graph bytes or operational ceremony." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-factory-qualification-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-graph-command-surface> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Register usf graph inspect, export and import with stable JSON help and receipts; require an explicit repository manifest and layer core or product, require an explicit versioned profile for product operations, reject ambiguous selections, and impose explicit byte, quad, item and elapsed-time bounds." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-graph-command-surface> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-graph-structural-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:qualificationPolicy> <urn:usf:policy:graph-structural-qualification:1> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-graph-structural-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Extend usf graph inspect with --detail summary or full over one explicit manifest, optional exact versioned profile and explicit core or product layer. Bind the exact manifest, profile, layer, semantic and directional digests, algorithm version and explicit quad, node, edge, item, byte and elapsed-time bounds. Compute deterministic quad, node, IRI-edge and predicate denominators; weak and strong components; typed in-degree and out-degree count, minimum, maximum, exact mean denominator, median, nearest-rank p95 and zero-degree counts; predicate and component-size frequencies; canonical duplicate and predicate-cardinality findings; typed profile, contract, work, requirement, acceptance, validation, evidence, proof, permission and state connectivity; profile closure and reachability; dependency and semantic-stage cycles, predecessor-first order, longest-path depth and per-level width; sound antichain lower and upper bounds without claiming exact maximum parallelism; write-set conflict edges and conflict-free frontier width; contract and work coverage; and declared core-product crossings. Summary returns complete counts, exact numerators and denominators and ratios without identity truncation; full adds lexically ordered bounded identities. Use linear O(Q + V + E) time and O(V + E) memory for the ordinary analysis. Never treat generic zero degree, catalogue presence, a descriptive statistic, Git state or a model judgement as completeness or construction authority." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-graph-structural-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-hermetic-reproducibility> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Make the accepted V3 semantic authority, source-selection contract, recovery inventory metadata, schemas, fixtures and validation inputs repository-contained and digest-bound. A clean third-party checkout may acquire the exact integrity-pinned lockfile artefact closure from the package registry allowed by GOAL.md, with install scripts disabled; after that bounded acquisition, semantic digests, validation, graph inspection and applicable unattended usf start, status and stop behavior reproduce offline without a warm cache, V1, V2 or Factory checkout, sibling Git repository, live Stardog, external CAS or database, GitHub API or hosted or self-hosted runner, provider credential, or network service. Historical repositories are optional explicitly supplied construction or re-audit inputs only: their absence cannot block ordinary build, test, runtime, BAU, currentness or acceptance; a rescan emits a bounded candidate diff and cannot mutate accepted authority. Repository-contained metadata proves integrity and internal coverage of the committed recovery result, while independent re-extraction of inaccessible historical bytes remains a separate nonclaim." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-hermetic-reproducibility> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-import-candidate-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Import accepts an explicitly bounded local input and format, parses and normalizes it to a candidate only, never edits a tracked graph or manifest, never publishes, and cannot make the candidate semantic authority without later explicit deterministic review and usf publish." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-import-candidate-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-inventory-command> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Register usf graph inventory --sources config/semantic-recovery-sources.json --source-root ID=PATH --compare-to PATH|none --out .usf/graph-inventory/FILE.json with repeated explicitly bound source roots and explicit accepted-baseline selection plus bounded byte, item and elapsed limits. Verify each supplied root against the operator-pinned revision and full tracked-tree closure, invoke only the graph-authorized exact-byte extractor, and emit a contained atomic owner-only candidate inventory plus complete added, removed and changed identity diff. The command never writes config/semantic-recovery-inventory.json, config/semantic-recovery.json or graph authority; rescans are optional construction or re-audit operations, and absence of historical roots cannot block ordinary coverage, build, test, runtime or BAU." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-inventory-command> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-layer-isolation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Keep reusable USF core definitions and versioned product overlays separate. Core export contains only core-authored named graphs. Product export contains only product-authored named graphs selected by an explicit versioned product profile and carries core dependencies as receipt digests rather than copied core graph bytes. Core authority must not acquire product triples or runtime coupling, and ANQR must receive its own evolving product graph and explicit profile." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-layer-isolation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-legacy-extraction-profile> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive recovery metadata from bounded exact source bytes inside src/graph/recovery-extract.ts; caller-authored quads, roles, record counts or self-hashed extraction receipts cannot establish completeness. Require raw pinned Git commit bytes plus every tracked path, mode and blob byte; recompute each Git blob identity, the recursive Git tree identity and the commit-to-tree binding before describing a source as independently extracted. Runtime authenticity uses private non-observable provenance rather than copyable properties, symbols or caller-recomputable digests. Support only the evidenced closure with exact integrity-locked parser versions: yaml 2.9.0 for strict YAML 1.2 and JSON, n3 2.0.1 for Turtle and TriG, and @traqula/parser-sparql-1-1 1.2.1 for parse-only SPARQL 1.1 rules. Disable YAML aliases, merge keys and custom tags; reject duplicate mapping keys, non-JSON JSON syntax and unsupported tags; impose positive safe-integer per-file and aggregate byte, node, depth, record, quad and elapsed limits; never execute rules or resolve remote references. Represent definition, authored, shape and derived graph files, observed collectors, rules with optional outputs, retired graphs with superseders, inactive digest-bound nonauthority sources and fixtures as a closed discriminated union; derive roles from section and path, preserve distinct load and validation order, permit repeated graph and order values, and reject only duplicate canonical entry identity or current-retired contradiction. Canonicalize parsed RDF metadata for stable definition and blank-node component digests while persisting only bounded identities, IRIs, counts and digests; unsupported or failed extraction remains an explicit unresolved candidate rather than a silent omission or an operational V3 ingestion path." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-legacy-extraction-profile> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-performance-ceilings> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Measure ten clean local runs and initially require 10,000-quad profile load and projection p95 no more than 250 milliseconds, affected validation p95 no more than 2 seconds, 100,000-quad full publication preparation no more than 15 seconds and 512 MiB RSS, and each model packet no more than 65,536 bytes; record any regression above 25 percent as a bottleneck decision rather than weakening bounds." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-performance-ceilings> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-recovery-denominator> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive the recovery denominator mechanically from every tracked artifact in the exact V1, V2 and readable Factory trees; every selected, derived, retired, inactive and fixture entry in their manifests and registries; all named semantic resources and relationship vocabulary in RDF; and all structured semantic instances, registries, schemas, taxonomies, vocabularies, tests and architecture or lineage documents rather than any hand-maintained domain or class list. This includes every kind and instance of contract, service, capability, requirement, policy, port, interface, connector, adapter, provider, environment, signal, assurance, test, shape, rule and lifecycle or action model without treating that enumeration as closed. Observability and telemetry, file and malware or virus scanning, database and persistence, test and environment postures, mail and notifications, identity authentication authorization and tenancy, ports interfaces connectors adapters and hexagonal boundaries, configuration and secret references, interaction events import export, evidence proof currentness invalidation, and deployment readiness backup restore upgrade rollback are required planted coverage witnesses only and never the inventory boundary." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-recovery-denominator> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-recovery-inventory> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Commit a frozen digest-bound metadata inventory at config/semantic-recovery-inventory.json and separately reviewed dispositions at config/semantic-recovery.json. Compiled coverage resolves exactly one deterministic disposition from re-express-ready, metadata-only, defer, not-claimed, historical-only, reject or unresolved for every tracked artifact in the pinned V1, V2 and readable Factory trees, every selected, derived, rule, retired, inactive and fixture manifest entry, every named semantic resource, RDF type assertion, predicate vocabulary term, referenced IRI, structured schema or registry record, test obligation and semantic document, including every Factory schema, entity, contract, service, action and record. Preserve source version, logical identity, evidence location, source and definition digests, exact source licence boundary, parser outcome, rationale, target V3 IRI, definition coverage state and operational implementation state. No inventory or disposition imports historical payload bytes or creates V3 authority. Automated V1 versus V2 comparison is only a raw source-identity delta; every claimed semantic split, merge, equivalence or replacement must be an explicit reviewed mapping." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-recovery-inventory> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-single-authority-path> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use graph-manifest version 2 import expansion, strict source validation and canonical dataset identity as the sole operational semantic ingestion path; unify or retire the incompatible semantic-store manifest path rather than maintaining two truths." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-single-authority-path> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-source-profile> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Select bootstrap-nquads-v1 as the only operational source profile: explicit named-graph, blank-node-free N-Quads with IRI subject, predicate and graph terms and IRI or untyped xsd:string object terms. Normalize every accepted lexical escape and line-ending variant to an RDFC-1.0-equivalent serialization for this subset while retaining exact source-byte digests separately. This deliberately supersedes only the Gate 1 Turtle and blank-node ingestion capability in docs/decisions/0001-semantic-store.md while retaining its disposable local store, bounded query and SHACL boundary; unsupported historical RDF remains recovery inventory evidence or a selective re-expression candidate rather than being silently discarded or adopted. A broader future profile requires an exact graph-defined V3 consumer, bounded standards-based canonicalization and migration without creating a second ingestion or identity path." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-source-profile> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-source-set-pin> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Pin exhaustiveness in the separately reviewed operator source-selection contract config/semantic-recovery-sources.json with schema urn:usf:semantic-recovery-source-set:1, integer version 1, exact immutable V1, V2 and every readable Factory release identity, full tracked-tree closure with no discovery-time inclusion filters, and the exact legacy manifests as additional graph indexes rather than scope limits. Define sourceSetDigest as sha256 over canonical JSON excluding only the sourceSetDigest field. The separately tracked accepted metadata inventory config/semantic-recovery-inventory.json and reviewed decisions config/semantic-recovery.json must both reference that digest but cannot create, widen or replace the source-selection contract; verification and coverage accept all three exact artifacts and refuse absent, coordinated omission, stale or mismatched schema, version, revision, tree, licence, manifest, closure, count, candidate or digest." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-recovery> .
